Coupler is a client for CoffeeMUD (coffeemud.net), by Bo Zimmerman and
its contributors. Its handling of the game's protocols follows Sip,
CoffeeMUD's own client by Bo Zimmerman (Apache License 2.0); no Sip
source is included.

Coupler includes:

- The Artisan class's skills, their levels and what each needs, taken
  from CoffeeMUD's source (Artisan.java and its skills), Copyright
  2003-2026 Bo Zimmerman (Apache License 2.0).
- The race and class portraits from CoffeeMUD's web pages
  (web/pub/images/mxp/race_*.jpg and web/pub/images/classes/), made
  into ANSI art by scripts/creation-art.py into
  public/creation-art.json and shown only when the player chooses them
  over Coupler's own painter, and the races' facts from its Races/*.java,
  Copyright 2000-2026 Bo Zimmerman (Apache License 2.0, as CoffeeMUD is
  distributed).
- IBM VGA 8x16 from The Ultimate Oldschool PC Font Pack by VileR
  (int10h.org/oldschool-pc-fonts), CC BY-SA 4.0, included unmodified
  with its license in public/fonts/ansiapps/.
- libopus, Copyright 2001-2023 Xiph.Org, Skype Limited, Octasic,
  Jean-Marc Valin, Timothy B. Terriberry, CSIRO, Gregory Maxwell, Mark
  Borgerding, Erik de Castro Lopo, Mozilla, Amazon (BSD 3-Clause).
- WavPack, Copyright (c) 1998-2022 David Bryant (BSD 3-Clause).
- flite-rs, a Rust implementation of CMU's Flite (Apache License 2.0),
  with speech data developed by Carnegie Mellon University and, in
  part, jointly by Carnegie Mellon University and the University of
  Edinburgh (CMU's license, in full in the licenses file).
- Pocket TTS by Kyutai (MIT), as ported to Rust by the Pocket TTS
  contributors (MIT), vendored and changed in
  src-tauri/vendor/pocket-tts (its README lists the changes). Its model
  is Kyutai's, CC BY 4.0, without the parts that clone a voice; its
  voices come from the VCTK corpus (University of Edinburgh) and Alba
  MacKenna (both CC BY 4.0), and from LibriVox readers and Kyutai's
  voice donations (CC0). The full credits ship with them, in the app's
  Resources/pocket-tts/CREDITS.txt.
- SQLite (public domain), and the Rust and npm libraries listed in
  Cargo.lock and package-lock.json under their own licenses.

Every third-party license text, in full, is in
public/third-party-licenses.txt (written by
scripts/third-party-licenses.py), and in the app under About ->
